#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "Quraysh had offered a reward for each of the two travellers. Suraqah ibn Malik recounts that a man came to his gathering and said he had just seen figures near the coast. Suraqah recognised who they must be, and set out after them."
msgstr "Quraysh had offered a reward for each of the two travellers. Suraqah ibn Malik recounts that a man came to his gathering and said he had just seen figures near the coast. Suraqah recognised who they must be, and set out after them."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "By his own account, he came close enough to hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. Then the forelegs of his horse sank into the ground up to the knees, and he was thrown from it."
msgstr "By his own account, he came close enough to hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. Then the forelegs of his horse sank into the ground up to the knees, and he was thrown from it."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "He told them what Quraysh intended and offered them provisions. They took nothing from him and asked only that he keep their news hidden. At his request, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah wrote him a guarantee of safety on a piece of leather. Then they went on."
msgstr "He told them what Quraysh intended and offered them provisions. They took nothing from him and asked only that he keep their news hidden. At his request, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah wrote him a guarantee of safety on a piece of leather. Then they went on."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "Quba: the first stop"
msgstr "Quba: the first stop"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "Then he rode on, with people walking beside him, until his camel knelt at a place in Madinah where some of the Muslims already prayed. It was a yard for drying dates."
msgstr "Then he rode on, with people walking beside him, until his camel knelt at a place in Madinah where some of the Muslims already prayed. It was a yard for drying dates."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "Suraqah’s account records the reward offered for each of the two, and a report that figures had been seen near the coast."
msgstr "Suraqah’s account records the reward offered for each of the two, and a report that figures had been seen near the coast."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "It does not establish where on the route this happened, and the scene does not place it."
msgstr "It does not establish where on the route this happened, and the scene does not place it."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "Suraqah describes the forelegs of his horse sinking into the ground to the knees, and being thrown."
msgstr "Suraqah describes the forelegs of his horse sinking into the ground to the knees, and being thrown."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "This is his own first-person account. The scene shows the road, not the event or any person."
msgstr "This is his own first-person account. The scene shows the road, not the event or any person."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "They asked only that he keep their news hidden; ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah wrote him a guarantee of safety."
msgstr "They asked only that he keep their news hidden; ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah wrote him a guarantee of safety."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "The wording of the written guarantee is not given in this passage."
msgstr "The wording of the written guarantee is not given in this passage."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "The account gives a stay of more than ten nights among Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf and the founding of a mosque there."
msgstr "The account gives a stay of more than ten nights among Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf and the founding of a mosque there."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "He rode on with people walking beside him until his camel knelt at the site of the mosque in Madinah."
msgstr "He rode on with people walking beside him until his camel knelt at the site of the mosque in Madinah."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "It does not establish the route taken through the town or the appearance of the place."
msgstr "It does not establish the route taken through the town or the appearance of the place."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "This excerpt does not give an exact departure date."
msgstr "This excerpt does not give an exact departure date."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "The excerpt describes preparations, not a nightly delivery to the cave."
msgstr "The excerpt describes preparations, not a nightly delivery to the cave."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "The excerpt does not describe erasing footprints."
msgstr "The excerpt does not describe erasing footprints."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "The account does not describe the cave’s dimensions or layout."
msgstr "The account does not describe the cave’s dimensions or layout."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "This excerpt is not the full verse and does not itself name Abu Bakr or Mount Thawr."
msgstr "This excerpt is not the full verse and does not itself name Abu Bakr or Mount Thawr."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "This is Ibn Kathir’s commentary, not the Quranic wording itself."
msgstr "This is Ibn Kathir’s commentary, not the Quranic wording itself."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "It does not give an exact location for the stay among Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf."
msgstr "It does not give an exact location for the stay among Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "The passage does not name the place; identifying it as Quba rests on other reports."
msgstr "The passage does not name the place; identifying it as Quba rests on other reports."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "The night of departure"
msgstr "The night of departure"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "The leaders of Quraysh met in Dar al-Nadwah, the house where they settled their affairs, to decide what to do about the Prophet ﷺ now that they feared him."
msgstr "The leaders of Quraysh met in Dar al-Nadwah, the house where they settled their affairs, to decide what to do about the Prophet ﷺ now that they feared him."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "That night they gathered at his door, waiting for him to sleep. He told ‘Ali to lie in his bed, wrapped in his green cloak, and assured him that no harm from them would reach him."
msgstr "That night they gathered at his door, waiting for him to sleep. He told ‘Ali to lie in his bed, wrapped in his green cloak, and assured him that no harm from them would reach him."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "The tent of Umm Ma‘bad"
msgstr "The tent of Umm Ma‘bad"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq reports that Quraysh met in Dar al-Nadwah to consult about the Prophet ﷺ once they feared him."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq reports that Quraysh met in Dar al-Nadwah to consult about the Prophet ﷺ once they feared him."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "The excerpt covers the meeting, not what was said in it."
msgstr "The excerpt covers the meeting, not what was said in it."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "They gathered at his door at night; he told ‘Ali to sleep in his bed under his green cloak and assured him of safety."
msgstr "They gathered at his door at night; he told ‘Ali to sleep in his bed under his green cloak and assured him of safety."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir notes that al-Waqidi also relates this, combining several narrators’ accounts."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir notes that al-Waqidi also relates this, combining several narrators’ accounts."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq introduces this with “as it has reached me”."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq introduces this with “as it has reached me”."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir calls the story well known, through routes that support one another. It does not fix where the tent stood."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir calls the story well known, through routes that support one another. It does not fix where the tent stood."

#: src/content/details.js
#: src/content/timeline.js
msgid "Al-Rahiq al-Makhtum"
msgstr "Al-Rahiq al-Makhtum"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "The noon visit"
msgstr "The noon visit"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "At the height of noon, an hour at which he never used to come, the Prophet ﷺ arrived at Abu Bakr’s house with his face covered. He said he had been given permission to leave. Abu Bakr asked to go with him, and he said yes."
msgstr "At the height of noon, an hour at which he never used to come, the Prophet ﷺ arrived at Abu Bakr’s house with his face covered. He said he had been given permission to leave. Abu Bakr asked to go with him, and he said yes."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "This is ‘Aishah’s account as quoted in a modern sirah. The position of the house is illustrative."
msgstr "This is ‘Aishah’s account as quoted in a modern sirah. The position of the house is illustrative."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Stones in the niche"
msgstr "Stones in the niche"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money with him, five or six thousand dirhams. Asma recounts that her blind grandfather feared the family had been left with nothing. She put stones where the money used to be kept, covered them with a cloth, and guided his hand to them so that he would be at ease."
msgstr "Abu Bakr took all his money with him, five or six thousand dirhams. Asma recounts that her blind grandfather feared the family had been left with nothing. She put stones where the money used to be kept, covered them with a cloth, and guided his hand to them so that he would be at ease."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Reported by Ibn Ishaq from Asma through her grandson. The position of the house is illustrative."
msgstr "Reported by Ibn Ishaq from Asma through her grandson. The position of the house is illustrative."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Why south?"
msgstr "Why south?"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Madinah lies to the north, and that is where a search would begin. They left in the opposite direction, on the road towards Yemen, for about five miles to Mount Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah lies to the north, and that is where a search would begin. They left in the opposite direction, on the road towards Yemen, for about five miles to Mount Thawr."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "This is a modern author’s reading of the route, not wording from an early report."
msgstr "This is a modern author’s reading of the route, not wording from an early report."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "She of the two belts"
msgstr "She of the two belts"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "When the three nights had passed, Asma brought their provisions but had forgotten a strap to hang the bag. She undid her waist-belt and used it. For that she was called Dhat al-Nitaqayn, she of the two belts."
msgstr "When the three nights had passed, Asma brought their provisions but had forgotten a strap to hang the bag. She undid her waist-belt and used it. For that she was called Dhat al-Nitaqayn, she of the two belts."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq’s report. ‘Aishah’s account in al-Bukhari places the belt at the packing of the provisions instead."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq’s report. ‘Aishah’s account in al-Bukhari places the belt at the packing of the provisions instead."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "The spider’s web"
msgstr "The spider’s web"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "One report says the pursuers climbed the mountain, passed the cave, and saw a spider’s web across its opening. No one could have gone in, they reasoned, and they moved on. Ibn Kathir calls its chain good, the best of what is reported on this. The scene does not draw the web."
msgstr "One report says the pursuers climbed the mountain, passed the cave, and saw a spider’s web across its opening. No one could have gone in, they reasoned, and they moved on. Ibn Kathir calls its chain good, the best of what is reported on this. The scene does not draw the web."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "A single report. The nesting doves of popular retellings are not part of it."
msgstr "A single report. The nesting doves of popular retellings are not part of it."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "The stations of the road"
msgstr "The stations of the road"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq names the way the guide took: below Makkah, along the coast, across the road below ‘Usfan, below Amaj, past Qudayd, then al-Kharrar, Thaniyyat al-Marah, Liqf and on. Many of these names are hard to place today, so the line drawn here stays approximate."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq names the way the guide took: below Makkah, along the coast, across the road below ‘Usfan, below Amaj, past Qudayd, then al-Kharrar, Thaniyyat al-Marah, Liqf and on. Many of these names are hard to place today, so the line drawn here stays approximate."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "A list of names, without distances or days."
msgstr "A list of names, without distances or days."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "White garments"
msgstr "White garments"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "On the way they met al-Zubayr with a group of Muslim merchants returning from Syria. He gave the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr white garments to wear."
msgstr "On the way they met al-Zubayr with a group of Muslim merchants returning from Syria. He gave the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr white garments to wear."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "From al-Bukhari, as quoted by Ibn Kathir. The account does not say where on the road they met."
msgstr "From al-Bukhari, as quoted by Ibn Kathir. The account does not say where on the road they met."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "The first Friday"
msgstr "The first Friday"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "After leaving Quba, the time for Friday prayer came while he was among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf. He led it there, in the mosque in the bed of the valley, with about a hundred men."
msgstr "After leaving Quba, the time for Friday prayer came while he was among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf. He led it there, in the mosque in the bed of the valley, with about a hundred men."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Quoted from a modern sirah, which cites Ibn Hisham. The position is illustrative."
msgstr "Quoted from a modern sirah, which cites Ibn Hisham. The position is illustrative."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Let her go"
msgstr "Let her go"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Clan after clan took hold of his camel’s rope and invited him to stay with them. Each time he answered: let her go, for she is under command. She walked on until she knelt in the quarter of Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Clan after clan took hold of his camel’s rope and invited him to stay with them. Each time he answered: let her go, for she is under command. She walked on until she knelt in the quarter of Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq’s report. Her path through the town is not known."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq’s report. Her path through the town is not known."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "The house of Abu Ayyub"
msgstr "The house of Abu Ayyub"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "He stayed in the house of Abu Ayyub until his mosque and his rooms were built, and he worked on the building himself alongside the Muhajirun and the Ansar."
msgstr "He stayed in the house of Abu Ayyub until his mosque and his rooms were built, and he worked on the building himself alongside the Muhajirun and the Ansar."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "The house is placed beside the mosque site for illustration."
msgstr "The house is placed beside the mosque site for illustration."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "Brothers"
msgstr "Brothers"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "He paired those who had migrated with those who received them, as brothers, so that each newcomer had someone to lean on."
msgstr "He paired those who had migrated with those who received them, as brothers, so that each newcomer had someone to lean on."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "This is Ibn Kathir’s chapter heading. The individual pairings are listed in the pages that follow it."
msgstr "This is Ibn Kathir’s chapter heading. The individual pairings are listed in the pages that follow it."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "The full moon has risen"
msgstr "The full moon has risen"

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "A well-known report says the women and children sang “The full moon has risen upon us, from the passes of al-Wada‘” when he arrived. Al-Bayhaqi relates it from Ibn ‘Aishah, a later narrator, not from someone who was there."
msgstr "A well-known report says the women and children sang “The full moon has risen upon us, from the passes of al-Wada‘” when he arrived. Al-Bayhaqi relates it from Ibn ‘Aishah, a later narrator, not from someone who was there."

#: src/content/details.js
msgid "The chain stops short of an eyewitness, and some place the song at a later return to Madinah, not at this arrival."
msgstr "The chain stops short of an eyewitness, and some place the song at a later return to Madinah, not at this arrival."

